1
00:00:00,023 --> 00:00:01,643
so how is UX research actually done?

2
00:00:01,643 --> 00:00:03,370
there There's user interview, where you sit

3
00:00:03,370 --> 00:00:04,830
down with people, you talk to them about

4
00:00:04,830 --> 00:00:06,330
their lives, their work, their frustration

5
00:00:06,330 --> 00:00:07,949
maybe how they use a product and all of that

6
00:00:07,949 --> 00:00:09,010
There's usability testing

7
00:00:09,010 --> 00:00:11,050
you give someone a task to do with your

8
00:00:11,050 --> 00:00:12,630
design maybe with your app, you watch how

9
00:00:12,630 --> 00:00:14,729
they do the tasks, usually while they think

10
00:00:14,729 --> 00:00:16,550
out loud then we have surveys

11
00:00:16,550 --> 00:00:18,090
you can reach a lot of people quickly with

12
00:00:18,090 --> 00:00:20,590
surveys but surveys usually have less depth

13
00:00:20,790 --> 00:00:22,670
and then there's contextual inquiry, where

14
00:00:22,670 --> 00:00:24,390
you go to where people work and live and

15
00:00:24,390 --> 00:00:26,059
watch them in their real environment

16
00:00:26,059 --> 00:00:28,530
there are also diary studies, where people

17
00:00:28,530 --> 00:00:31,330
record their experiences over days or weeks

18
00:00:31,330 --> 00:00:33,650
so you see patterns that maybe a single

19
00:00:33,650 --> 00:00:34,800
session would have missed
